/// The questions that are asked about a picture.
///
/// Every one of these carries a `figure` id naming a drawing in
/// quiz_figures.dart. They were written together, in one source that
/// produced both the painter calls and a contact sheet of all 145 figures,
/// so a question and its picture cannot drift apart -- and so that every
/// figure could be looked at before it shipped.
///
/// Most are maths, and deliberately: NJ's father taught the subject to
/// tenth to twelfth formers for a working lifetime. Geometry, fractions,
/// clock faces and the reading of a scale are the things he knows best and
/// has known longest, which is exactly the ground a memory losing its
/// recent layers keeps hold of. A question about a shape also asks nothing
/// of his reading or his recall -- the whole question is on the screen in
/// front of him.
///
/// Answer positions cycle 0, 1, 2, 3.
